IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Schedule III (repealed) and Schedule IV (paragraph 12(7)(a)): the Number of
-- Weeks of Benefits Conversion Table. Written by piece ei6 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24; the rows below were generated by a
-- script that reads the raw file (src:3434-3494), so no figure is typed by hand. Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering
-- of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- What the table decides: when benefits have been paid for the care of a new-born or adopted child and the 61-week maximum
-- was elected (subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii), at the 33% rate), the weeks paid are converted to the weeks that would have been
-- paid at the 55% rate, to see whether the total of 50 combined weeks (s 12(6), (7); piece ei1) has been reached. A number of
-- weeks that is not a whole number from 1 to 61 has no row, so it is NOTHING (the text gives none).

§ `Schedule III - repealed`

